From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:19:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: refuse submits on a failed queue and latch on
 retirement errors

A queue latched by a rejected command still accepted new submissions,
which could only complete with ECANCELED. Refuse them in the SUBMIT ioctl
with ECANCELED, as xe and amdgpu do for a banned queue or lost context.
Honeykrisp already reports any submit failure as device loss.

A command that completes with an error at retirement (a render that hit
its TVB memory limit, ENOMEM) failed only its own job. Later jobs on the
same queue may already be published, so the publication latch cannot stop
them; they would signal success over incomplete output, and Honeykrisp
only inspects the queue's latest timeline point. Latch the queue on any
retirement error and complete every later job on it with ECANCELED.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
